# Who may be on the bus, as what, what each may send, and what it hears.
# SECURITY.txt §5.
#
#   <certificate CN>  <node>  node   [<may send>...]  [hears <announcement>...]
#   <certificate CN>  <node>  panel
#
# A certificate not listed here may not connect. A node is one
# certificate's — a second line for the same node is an error — and holds
# one connection: a second, while the first is up, is refused and logged.
#
# A pattern is written as a grant is: an action, or a prefix of one ending
# in "*". What a node sends is TO.VERB.NOUN. Without a pattern it may answer
# what it is asked and announce its own PUB and REG to ALL; anything else
# must be listed. It is given every request put to it; of what others
# announce — PUB, REG, FIRE, written FROM.VERB.NOUN — only what follows
# "hears".
#
# A panel is a person's door, and lists nothing. It may do nothing but sign
# in until it shows the hub a ticket marshal signed for its person; then it
# speaks as <node>.<person>, sends what the ticket's grants cover, and hears
# the announcements they cover.
#
# The bus carries monolink v2 only (SPEC §44). A node still sending v1 is
# connected, and every frame it sends is dropped.
#
# After editing: kill -HUP the concentrator. Whoever the new policy no
# longer admits as they were is dropped at once.

achtung        ACHTUNG    node    ALL.FIRE.* VERTEX.SET.BUZZ.STATE
governor       GOVERNOR   node
marshal        MARSHAL    node    UKAZ.PRINT.*
synapse        SYNAPSE    node    MARSHAL.GET.PEOPLE    hears MARSHAL.PUB.PEOPLE
ukaz           UKAZ       node    GOVERNOR.GET.* ACHTUNG.GET.UPTIME VERTEX.GET.UPTIME    hears ACHTUNG.FIRE.*
vertex         VERTEX     node    # uart2ws, for vertex

portal         MONOWEB    panel
monoview       MONOVIEW   panel
# Two monoviews cannot share MONOVIEW: a node is one certificate's.
